# Approval gates

Stop and ask before any of the following. Prior chat approval does not widen scope.

## Always require approval

- `git commit`, `git push`, creating/updating PRs on the remote
- **Production DB**: connect, read, write, migrate, restore-into-prod
- **Shared/development DB**: connect, read, write, migrate (read also requires approval)
- **Production branch Merge** (even if Ruleset allows merge with 0 reviews)
- **Production Deploy** and production env var changes
- Fetching, printing, or pasting secrets / credentials / dump passphrases / DB URLs
- Deleting existing user/business data
- Changing or deleting USB backups
- Host changes outside the approved sandbox (global PATH, existing PGDATA, unrelated package upgrades)
- Changing Vercel/auto-deploy configuration without explicit approval

## Merge vs Deploy

- Track Merge approval and Deploy approval **separately**.
- If merging to the Production branch **automatically triggers** Production Deploy, obtain Deploy approval **before** Merge. **Do not Merge without Deploy approval** in that configuration.
- If auto-Deploy is inseparable from Merge, obtain **both** approvals, then Merge.
- Do not change auto-Deploy settings to bypass this rule.

## Allowed without new approval (typical)

- Local code edits in the assigned worktree
- Local tests/builds against a **fully isolated disposable local DB** only when the current task already allows it
- Draft docs / agent-store notes (no secrets)
- Read-only `gh` inspection of Issues/PRs/checks/rulesets

## On block

Report with the standard template (`Approval Required:` filled). Do not invent workarounds that bypass the gate (force-push, stash of foreign dirty trees, audit-threshold relaxation, `automerge` label).
